  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "A parabola passes through the points $(a,0)$, $(b,0)$ and $(0,c)$, where $a\\ne b$, $ab\\ne0$ and $c\\ne0$. Find the equation of the parabola in intercept form.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=\\frac{c}{ab}(x-a)(x-b)$\n\nUse the two intercepts, then substitute $(0,c)$ to determine the coefficient.",
      "worked": "The intercepts give $y=K(x-a)(x-b)$. Substitute $(0,c)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}c&=K(0-a)(0-b)\\\\c&=Kab\\\\K&=\\frac{c}{ab}\\\\y&=\\frac{c}{ab}(x-a)(x-b).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
